Software that is not redistributed
----------------------------------
- Codex CLI (OpenAI, Apache-2.0). Runs are executed through the official
  `codex app-server`, which you install yourself; DerivationLab requires
  version 0.147.0 exactly. The file
  src/derivation_runtime/protocol_schema/codex_app_server_protocol.v2.schemas.json
  is the app-server protocol schema generated from Codex CLI 0.147.0, kept so
  the tests can check the client against the protocol it pins.
- Tectonic (MIT) and its TeX resource bundle. PDF reporting uses Tectonic
  0.17.0 with the default bundle v33 and the Fandol CJK fonts. None of it is in
  this repository: tools/provision_tectonic.py downloads it and verifies it
  against config/reporting/tectonic_runtime.lock.json and
  config/reporting/tectonic_bundle_manifest.json (file names and digests only).
  Those components remain under their own licences: MIT for Tectonic itself;
  the LaTeX Project Public License, the SIL Open Font License 1.1, the GUST
  Font License and others for the bundle's packages and fonts; GPL-3.0 with the
  font exception for Fandol.


